# PREFETCH—Prefetch L1 Data-Cache Line (AMD 3DNow! prefetch; not in the Intel SDM)
# AMD64 Architecture Programmer's Manual Vol. 3, "PREFETCH / PREFETCHW":
# 0F 0D /0 is PREFETCH, /1 PREFETCHW (its own page), and the other ModRM.reg
# encodings are reserved hints that execute as PREFETCH. A prefetch never
# faults and has no architectural effect (v1 has no caches); the register
# form is #UD (memory operands only). CPUID 8000_0001h:ECX[8] 3DNowPrefetch.
@opcodes
0F 0D /0 | PREFETCH m8 | M | Valid | Valid
0F 0D /2 | PREFETCH m8 | M | Valid | Valid
0F 0D /3 | PREFETCH m8 | M | Valid | Valid
0F 0D /4 | PREFETCH m8 | M | Valid | Valid
0F 0D /5 | PREFETCH m8 | M | Valid | Valid
0F 0D /6 | PREFETCH m8 | M | Valid | Valid
0F 0D /7 | PREFETCH m8 | M | Valid | Valid
@encoding
M | ModRM:r/m (r) | N/A | N/A | N/A
@operation
@flags
None.
